(opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-670" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">November 18, 2026 Utah Valley Road Special Service District Notice of Public Hearing</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">October 27, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice-226-830UVRoadSSD-1.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about November 18, 2026 Utah Valley Road Special Service District Notice of Public Hearing (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-669" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">November 18, 2026 Municipal Building Authority of Utah County Notice of Public Hearing</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">October 27, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice-2026-842-MBA-1.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about November 18, 2026 Municipal Building Authority of Utah County Notice of Public Hearing (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-667" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">November 18, 2026 Utah County Community Reinvestment Agency Notice of Public Hearing</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">October 27, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="/api/media/file/notice2026-832cra.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about November 18, 2026 Utah County Community Reinvestment Agency Notice of Public Hearing (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-666" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Alys O’Brien October 2026 Employee of the Month</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">October 26, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Alys O’Brien is Utah County&#x27;s Employee of the Month for September 2026.  Her work helps ensure that Utah County’s records are accurate, up to date, and useful to the people who rely on them. Since joining the Utah County Assessor’s Office in August 2023, she has brought real estate experience, a strong sense of responsibility, and a collaborative approach to her work.</p>
<p>One of Alys’s major responsibilities is coordinating building permits from 28 jurisdictions throughout the county. In 2025, she received and processed 10,827 permits. For each one, she identifies key information and routes it to the appropriate field appraiser. That work helps the Assessor’s Office track new construction, maintain an accurate tax roll, and account for growth across Utah County.</p>
<p>Alys is also proactive about getting the information the office needs. If permits are missing or a city’s submissions are delayed, she follows up with city personnel and her supervisor to help make sure nothing is overlooked. She is currently working with a data analyst to explore using AI software to extract relevant information from permits more efficiently.
Her attention to detail benefits colleagues across the county, too. A GIS Division employee who maintains address points used in the 911 system praised Alys for entering clean, accurate address information and keeping them informed about changes. When questions or errors come up, Alys is helpful and solutions-oriented, either resolving the issue herself or connecting the employee with someone who can.</p>
<p>Alongside these responsibilities, Alys assists residents at the front counter and answers incoming calls. Colleagues describe her as pleasant, dependable, and easy to work with. She brings a sense of humor to the office, while staying focused when it’s time to get the work done.</p>
<p>Much of Alys’s contribution happens behind the scenes, but its impact is clear. Her diligence supports accurate records, responsive service, and the important work of the Assessor’s Office. Congratulations, Alys, and thank you for all you do for Utah County!</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-665" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">October 29, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, UT Budget Work Session</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">October 23, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Board members may participate electronically, when necessary, with the anchor location designated as stated above.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-664" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">October 28, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, UT Budget Work Session</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">October 23, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Board members may participate electronically, when necessary, with the anchor location designated as stated above.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-663" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">October 27, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, UT Budget Work Session</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">October 23, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Board members may participate electronically, when necessary, with the anchor location designated as stated above.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-662" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-