se break-words content-flow"><p>View Agenda: <a href="https://www.utahcounty.gov/cms/uploads/October_TTAB_Agenda_37862cb479.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.utahcounty.gov/cms/uploads/October_TTAB_Agenda_37862cb479.pdf<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-632" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Notice of Vacancy - North Utah County Water Conservancy District</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 24, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>NOTICE OF VACANCY ON THE NORTH UTAH COUNTY WATER CONSERVANCY DISTRICT BOARD OF TRUSTEES </p>
<p>Notice is hereby provided this 23rd day of September 2026, pursuant to Utah Code Sections I 7B-l-304 and I 7B-2a-l 005, that one (I) vacancy currently exist on the North Utah County Water Conservancy District Board of Trustees (the ·&#x27;Board&quot;), to fill one (I) expired term. Positions on the Board are for individuals who are representatives of a specific geographical area or interest. </p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice_2026_743_d45a9b6791.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Notice of Vacancy - North Utah County Water Conservancy District (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-616" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Notice of Vacancy - North County Water Conservancy District Board of Trustees</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 24, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>NOTICE OF VACANCY ON THE NORTH UTAH COUNTY WATER CONSERVANCY DISTRICT BOARD OF TRUSTEES </p>
<p>Notice is hereby provided this 23rd day of September 2026, pursuant to Utah Code Sections I 7B-l-304 and I 7B-2a-l 005, that one (I) vacancy currently exist on the North Utah County Water Conservancy District Board of Trustees (the ·&#x27;Board&quot;), to fill one (I) expired term. Positions on the Board are for individuals who are representatives of a specific geographical area or interest. </p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice_2026_743_02294f7b25.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Notice of Vacancy - North County Water Conservancy District Board of Trustees (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-641" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">September 24, 2026 Utah County Career Service Council Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 23, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PUBLIC NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN THAT THE </p>
<p><strong>UTAH COUNTY CAREER SERVICE COUNCIL</strong></p>
<p>WILL HOLD A PUBLIC MEETING</p>
<p>IN THE THIRD-FLOOR CONFERENCE ROOM– SUITE 3800</p>
<p>OF THE UTAH COUNTY ADMINISTRATION BUILDING</p>
<p>100 East Center Street, Provo, Utah</p>
<p><strong>September 24, 2026 – 5:30 P.M.</strong></p>
<p><em>(The order of this agenda is subject to change at the discretion of the Council.)</em>                                                      </p>
<p><strong>AGENDA</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>APPROVE RESOLUTION ESTABLISHING GUIDELINES AND OPERATING PROCEDURES FOR APPEAL HEARINGS</li>
<li>CONDUCT PRE-HEARING MEETING FOR DIANA JOHNSON APPEAL </li>
<li>APPROVE AND SET A DATE, TIME AND LOCATION FOR A CLOSED MEETING TO DISCUSS THE CHARACTER, PROFESSIONAL COMPETENCE, OR PHYSICAL OR MENTAL HEALTH OF AN INDIVIDUAL OR INDIVIDUALS FOR TODAY’S DATE, AT THIS LOCATION, AS NEEDED. </li>
</ol>
<p><em>In compliance with the American Disabilities Act, individuals needing special accommodations (including auxiliary communicative aids and service) during this meeting should notify the Utah County Human Resources at (801) 851-8158 at least one day prior to the meeting.</em></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-607" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">September 23, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 22, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1998" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about September 23, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/BOE_Agenda_2026_09_23_aa7f5d61ae.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about September 23, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-638" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">September 23, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 21, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1900" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about September 23, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Commission_Agenda_2026_09_23_de49887208.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about September 23, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-640" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Sgt. Zac Robinson September 2026 Employee of the Month</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 18, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Sgt. Zac Robinson is Utah County&#x27;s Employee of the Month for September 2026.  He is a leader, mentor, and brings strategic contributions to both the Utah County Search and Rescue (SAR) Team and the county’s aviation program.</p>
<p>In 2026, he took on the responsibility of training a group of 10 new members, investing hours of expertise to ensure they are well-prepared to excel in their roles. His commitment to fostering talent reflects a deep-rooted dedication to the team’s long-term success and continuity.</p>
<p>Beyond training, Sgt. Robinson has been instrumental in guiding the aviation unit’s growth and future direction. Over the past several months, he has led the effort to research and evaluate aircraft options to ensure the Sheriff’s Office selects a platform that best meets the unit’s operational needs. This work required extensive analysis, coordination with industry professionals, and a thorough understanding of mission requirements. </p>
<p>He devoted countless hours to comparing performance data, safety features, cost considerations, and operational versatility, delivering clear, well-supported recommendations that will influence the future effectiveness of Utah County’s aviation operations.</p>
<p>The excellence in his work is underscored by the ongoing process of acquiring a DA62 MPP aircraft. This aircraft is expected to provide enhanced service and a greater sense of security to the citizens of Utah County, a goal aligned with Sgt. Robinson’s commitment to public safety and operational readiness.</p>
<p>His contributions and dedication make him a highly deserving candidate for recognition as Employee of the Month.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-639" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Notice of Vacancies on the Springville Drainage District Board of Trustees</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 18, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>NOTICE OF VACANCIES ON THE SPRINGVILLE DRAINAGE DISTRICT BOARD OF TRUSTEES</p>
<p>Notice is hereby provided this 16th day of September 2026, pursuant to Utah Code Section 17B-1-304 that three (3) vacancies currently exist on the Springville Drainage District Board of Trustees (the “Board”). To be qualified for consideration for the above-mentioned Board vacancies, the individuals (i) must be a registered voter at the location of the member’s residence, and (ii) a resident residing within the boundaries of the Springville Drainage District (the “District”) or an officer or employee of Utah County. The individuals interested in being considered for the vacant Board positions outlined above should send a letter expressing their interest, together with a brief description of their qualifications and eligibility for the Board positions to: <a href="mailto:boards@utahcounty.gov">boards@utahcounty.gov</a>. All letters of interest in the vacant Board positions must be received by the Board of County Commissioners, Utah County, Utah, on or before 5:00 p.m. on Friday, October 30, 2026. The Board of County Commissioners, Utah County, Utah, will review and evaluate all individuals that qualify for consideration pursuant to the guidelines listed above and will appoint individuals to fill the vacancies by resolution.</p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice_2026_724_8045506146.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Notice of Vacancies on the Springville Drainage District Board of Trustees (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-636" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Notice of Logic and Accuracy Testing - October 1, 2026</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 18, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>NOTICE OF LOGIC AND ACCURACY TESTING</p>
<p>In accordance with Utah Code § 20A-4-104(1), the Utah County Clerk will conduct a logic and accuracy test of automatic tabulating equipment prior to the General Election to be held on November 3rd, 2026, for Utah County’s federal, state, and county races. The logic and accuracy test is open to the public and will be held on Thursday, October 1, 2026, at 10:00 AM Mountain Time at the following location:<br/>
<!-- --> </p>
<p>Utah County Administration Building<br/>
<!-- -->Ballot Processing Center<br/>
<!-- -->100 E Center Street, Room LL700<br/>
<!-- -->Provo, UT 84606<br/>
<!-- --> </p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/L_and_A_Public_Notice_1_7ff1550b8b.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Notice of Logic and Accuracy Testing - October 1, 2026 (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-637" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">First Down Provo...a Resounding Success!</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 17, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PROVO, Utah — First Down Provo was an event designed to turn a football game day experience into a multi-day “game weekend” as well as boost economic activity in downtown Provo.</p>
<p>Utah County Commissioner Skyler Beltran said the gathering was meant to bring the community downtown and bring them together and cheer on the nationally ranked BYU Cougars, so Utah County along with Explore Utah Valley, Provo City, Downtown Provo, BYU Athletics and BYU Alumni Relations organized this event and it was a resounding success!</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-633" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Sample Ballot for the November 3, 2026 General Election</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 17, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>In accordance with Utah Code 20A-5-405(f)(iii): The following is the Amended 2026 General Sample Ballot. </p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/2026_General_Sample_Ballots_Corrected_2_e50150f2c0.PDF" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Amended 2026 General Sample Ballot<span class="sr-only"> about Sample Ballot for the November 3, 2026 General Election (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-635" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">On Demand Service Helps Keep Seniors Independent</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 16, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>The UTA On-Demand service offers seniors rides for $1.25 each way and more importantly, helping elderly residents stay more independent. </p>
<p>Vanetta Levao, has been using the service in Ogden for years and said the service lets her do more than “sit at home and watch TV.” There’s a lot of people that can use it, like her sister Faafofoga Suamataia whom she is showing how to use the service, now that it&#x27;s in Utah County. “It’s helpful to us that are less independent.” She added that she and others can accomplish more with the rides, including trips to religious services and running errands.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-615" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">September 16, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 15, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1997" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about September 16, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/BOE_Agenda_2026_09_16_9ad7d63dbc.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about September 16, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-606" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">September 16, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 14, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1899" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about September 16, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Commission_Agenda_2026_09_16_e393b01cf1.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about September 16, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-628" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">September 15, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Budget Work Session</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 14, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PUBLIC NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN THAT THE </p>
<p><strong>BOARD OF COMMISSIONERS OF UTAH COUNTY, UTAH</strong> WILL HOLD A BUDGET WORK SESSION</p>
<p>AT THE RUTH THEATER 401 S PLEASANT GROVE BLVD, PLEASANT GROVE, UTAH 84062</p>
<p><strong>September 15, 2026 - 10:00 AM</strong></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Work_Session_Agenda_2026_09_15_3f30817bc3.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="sr-only"> about September 15, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Budget Work Session (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-634" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">United Way Day of Caring </h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 10, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PROVO, Utah - Utah County Commissioners were a part of United Way Day of Caring, a countywide effort that mobilizes volunteers from local businesses to support libraries, schools and other community programs.</p>
<p>Utah County Commissioner, Skyler Beltran, volunteered to flip pancakes at the morning kickoff.  He served volunteers who gathered to eat before heading out to service projects across the county. “We are serving breakfast for all the volunteers,” he said, noting that the hearty meal helps start a day of work in the community.</p>
<p>Beltran said the event is designed to bring the community together and set a collaborative tone for the day. “It brings all the community together,” he said.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-630" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">First Down Provo to debut as new pregame event in downtown Provo</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 10, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PROVO, Utah — A new pregame event called First Down Provo will debut Friday, September 11th 2026, bringing live music, food trucks, inflatable play areas and a charity canned food drive to downtown Provo ahead of BYU’s first Big 12 conference game of the season, Utah County Commissioner Skyler Beltran said.</p>
<p>Center Street will be closed from University to 100 East for the downtown event, with most activities taking place on the County Historic Courthouse campus. The lineup includes food trucks, a live band, BYU Store and concessions stands, and a canned food drive to benefit Community Action Services and Food Bank. The event, will also have in attendance, the Provo Fire Department to commemorate 9/11, Beltran said.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-631" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Nicole Stevens Honored with the Pillar of Democracy Award</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 9, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Elections Director, Nicole Stevens was honored with the Pillar of Democracy Award at Utah’s Excellence in Elections Award Banquet. <br/>
<!-- --> <br/>
<!-- -->The words on the certificate say it perfectly: <br/>
<!-- --> <br/>
<!-- -->“In recognition of her extraordinary mentorship, generosity, and swift support, and for her steadfast dedication to empowering neighboring election offices. By volunteering her time, sharing resources, and providing critical equipment during crises, she exemplifies the highest spirit of collaboration and public service in Utah elections.” <br/>
<!-- --> <br/>
<!-- -->Elections are never the work of one person or one office. Behind every election are people sharing knowledge, answering calls, solving problems, loaning equipment, stepping in when another office needs help, and doing whatever it takes to serve voters.  Nicole has always believed that when another election office needs help, help is provided. County lines don’t change that. <br/>
<!-- --> <br/>
<!-- -->Utah County is proud that Nicole has been recognized for her mentorship, collaboration, and for supporting her fellow election officials. Those are values she works hard to live by on a daily basis. County Commissioner Amelia Powers Gardner wrote a letter recognizing Nicole (Nikki), sharing a story of a time in 2023, when she and her colleague Jenn offered their expertise and taught staff the essentials of administering an election. Scroll to the accompanying images to read the letter.</p>
<p>She often emphasizes that she can’t do it without her amazing team, whose hard work, support, and unwavering spirit form the backbone of this success.<br/>
<!-- --> <br/>
<!-- -->“I love this profession. I love the people I get to work alongside. And I’m incredibly proud of the work we do. I am honored to work under Lt. Governor Deidre Henderson and her amazing staff! They make Utah Elections possible.” - Nicole Stevens  <br/>
<!-- --> <br/>
<!-- -->Nicole Stevens, on behalf of everyone at Utah County, you epitomize the Pillar of Democracy. Congratulations!</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-629" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">UTA On-Demand Service Solves Utah County’s Last Mile Issue</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 8, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>SARATOGA SPRINGS, Utah — The UTA on-demand ride-share service is helping Utah County residents bridge the last mile between FrontRunner and everyday destinations.</p>
<p>The service is designed to connect people from major transit hubs to homes, offices and shops in a growing region. A Utah County residents we talked to, described the concept as a flexible alternative to car travel, especially for those who rely on trains to reach Salt Lake City or who share a single vehicle.</p>
<p>“I always like options on how I can get around,” AJ Averett said. “Being able to go to Salt Lake, it’s been nice to use the train, but coordinating between my wife and I because we only have one car is sometimes annoying. The micro transit service is pretty cool. I am big on whatever can get me from A to B. I’m a big fan of it.”</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-627" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Utah County expands UTA Connect to tackle last-mile transit</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 4, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>UTAH COUNTY, Utah — Utah County will expand the UTA Connect on-demand ride-share program to address the last mile of public transit, linking FrontRunner stations and other hubs to homes, work and errands in a fast-growing region.</p>
<p>“In the transit and transportation world, that is the distance from your main transit hub,” Utah County Commissioner Skyler Beltran said, explaining the term last mile. “How do we get people from those locations to their home or to the service that they are using or to their job, which is typically within a couple miles? And this connects them from the main hub to where they need to go?”</p>
<p>The expansion targets Eagle Mountain, Saratoga Springs, Lehi and a portion of American Fork, with the aim of easing congestion as the county’s population swells. Beltran described the plan as a proactive step to begin building ridership for UTA and public transit in a region where traffic and gridlock are persistent issues.</p>
<p>“This on-demand service will allow you in Eagle Mountain, Saratoga, Lehi to go within six miles,” Beltran said, adding that there is no cap if you travel to the Lehi or American Fork FrontRunner stations, which links riders into the broader network.</p>
<p>Officials emphasize that UTA Connect is not intended to compete with private ride-hailing services. Beltran highlighted several differentiators: a network that keeps trips within the UTA system and a shared-ride model that pools riders headed in similar directions.</p>
<p>“We do not want to compete with the private sector; there are key differences—the network connection within the UTA system and the shared ride,” he said.</p>
<p>Riders will pay $2.50 per trip, with service available within two hours of a ride request. The fare allows trips from city centers to FrontRunner stations or across the network, and trips can be requested through the On Demand UTA app, which will indicate the driver’s arrival time and availability.</p>
<p>“It is two dollars and fifty cents,” Beltran said, with a note that the app makes the service simple and intuitive to hail and track.</p>
<p>The move comes as Utah County anticipates continued rapid growth. Beltran noted that Eagle Mountain was the ninth-fastest growing city in the United States in 2025, and the expanded service area will reach about 180,000 people across Saratoga Springs, Lehi and Eagle Mountain, all while roughly $1.5 billion in road projects proceed concurrently.</p>
<p>Beltran argued the shift could boost mobility for students, people with disabilities and the elderly, potentially reducing car trips and easing gridlock as the region expands. He cited examples of local families already benefiting from on-demand options and emphasized the broader economic and mobility advantages of the program.</p>
<p>Officials say the rollout aims to improve access to work, education and essential services while moving the county closer to managing growth in a way that keeps people connected and reduces congestion.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-623" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Amending the Annual Regular Meeting Schedule for the Board of County Commissioners of Utah County, Utah</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 4, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>RESOLUTION AMENDING THE ANNUAL REGULAR MEETING SCHEDULE FOR THE BOARD OF COUNTY COMMISSIONERS OF UTAH COUNTY, UTAH, FOR THE YEAR 2026</p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Resolution_2026_701_95fae7c1dd.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Resolution and Meeting Schedule<span class="sr-only"> about Amending the Annual Regular Meeting Schedule for the Board of County Commissioners of Utah County, Utah (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-614" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Notice of Public Hearing - September 23, 2026</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 4, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>NOTICE OF PUBLIC HEARING</p>
<p>In accordance with Utah Code Sections 17-36-23, 17-36-24, and 17-36-26, the Board of County Commissioners, Utah County, Utah will hold a public hearing on Wednesday, September 23, 2026 at 2:00 p.m. at the Utah County Administration Building, 100 East Center Street, Room 1400, Provo, Utah, to consider amending the budgets in the County&#x27;s general fund and various other budgetary funds; to consider revisions to the County&#x27;s estimates of revenues; to consider revising the budget appropriations of county departments; and/or to consider transferring unencumbered or unexpected appropriation balances from one department in a fund to another department in the same fund. After the public hearing the Board of County Commissioners, Utah County, Utah, may amend the 2026 County&#x27;s general fund budget and the various other County budgetary funds, may revise the County&#x27;s estimates of revenues, may revise the budget appropriations of county departments, and/or may transfer unencumbered or unexpended appropriation balances from one department in a fund to another department in the same fund.</p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice_2026_702_2eb0a33ae1.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Notice of Public Hearing - September 23, 2026 (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-613" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Huntsman Cancer Institute to open Vineyard campus, boosting cancer care across Utah County</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 3, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>VINEYARD, Utah — Huntsman Cancer Institute held a Cornerstone Celebration this week.  The Comprehensive Cancer Center campus in Vineyard, is expected to open in the fall of 2028. Located in one of the fastest-growing regions in the United States, this 272,000-square-foot facility will provide advanced cancer care closer to patients in Utah County and nearby communities, thereby significantly reducing the time required for treatment.</p>
<p>Bradley Cairns, chief executive officer of Huntsman Cancer Institute, opened the announcement by thanking partners and outlining the mission behind the project. “We are building the center in Vineyard for you and with you. We are grateful for our many partners such as the Utah County Commissioners, Utah County Mayors, and Utah County Health Department,” Cairns said.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-622" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">2026 General Election Candidate Certification</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 2, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>In accordance with Utah Code 20A-5a-210: The following candidates won their respective primary races held during the Primary Election or filed to run for an office not requiring a primary and are officially certified to appear on the General Election ballot on November 3, 2026.</p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Utah_County_2026_General_Election_Candidate_Certification_4e705c1719.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View 2026 General Election Candidate Certification<span class="sr-only"> about 2026 General Election Candidate Certification (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-612" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">September 2, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">September 1, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1996" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about September 2, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/BOE_Agenda_2026_09_02_16f6e62155.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about September 2, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-605" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">September 2, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 31, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1898" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about September 2, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Commission_Agenda_2026_09_02_ecaf786d69.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about September 2, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-23" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">UTA - Rideshare Program Off To A Great Start</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 27, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Today Utah County celebrated the success of the UTA On-Demand Service with our two partners...Utah Transit Authority and UDOT.</p>
<p>More than 1000 people rode the service in the first 9 days! Amazing number that proves that public transit in Utah County is wanted and needed.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-621" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">August 28, 2026 Utah County Criminal Justice Coordinating Council</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 27, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PUBLIC NOTICE IS HEARBY GIVEN THAT THE UTAH COUNTY CRIMINAL JUSTICE COORDINATING COUNCIL WILL HOLD A PUBLIC MEETING AT 51 SOUTH UNIVERSITY AVE., PROVO, UTAH 84601 IN THE HISTORIC COURTHOUSE, 3rd FLOOR COMMISSION CONFERENCE ROOM</p>
<p>August 28, 2026 – 12:00 p.m.</p>
<p>The public may participate at the anchor location stated above. Public comments will be limited to two (2) minutes <br/>
<!-- -->per individual unless otherwise approved by the Board.</p>
<p>AGENDA<br/>
<!-- -->1. Welcome<br/>
<!-- -->-Jeff Gray<br/>
<!-- -->2. Approve previous meeting minutes<br/>
<!-- -->3. Discuss status of pretrial services<br/>
<!-- -->4. Discuss Council goals and next projects<br/>
<!-- -->5. Next Meeting Date &amp; Adjourn<br/>
<!-- --> </p>
<p>PUBLIC COMMENTS</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-611" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Sleeping Mat Campaign Update</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 26, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Our “250 Sleeping Mats” campaign got off to a great start!  Thanks to your generosity we collected 100 mats in 8 days!  Amazing!  Our goal is to provide 250 new sleeping mats for this year’s Utah County Warming Center before it opens on November 1.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-619" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Utah County designates August as Breastfeeding Month</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 25, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>UTAH COUNTY, Utah — The Utah County Board of Commissioners designated August as Utah County Breastfeeding Month, continuing a designation the county has adopted each year for the past five years. The recognition highlights the important role breastfeeding plays in supporting the health of mothers and infants and encourages greater access to resources for families.</p>
<p>The American Academy of Pediatrics recommends exclusive breastfeeding for approximately the first six months of life, followed by continued breastfeeding alongside complementary foods. Breastfeeding provides nutrition tailored to infants, supports healthy growth and immune development, and can reduce the risk of certain illnesses. Mothers may also experience important health benefits, including improved postpartum recovery and reduced risk of some cancers.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-610" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">August 26, 2026 Utah County Capital Improvement Plan Committee Public Work Session</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 21, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PUBLIC NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN THAT THE UTAH COUNTY CAPITAL IMPROVEMENT PLAN COMMITTEE </p>
<p>WILL HOLD A PUBLIC WORK SESSION IN SUITE 3600, AUDITOR CONFERENCE ROOM OF THE UTAH COUNTY ADMINISTRATION</p>
<p>BUILDING 100 EAST CENTER STREET, PROVO, UTAH </p>
<p>August 26, 2026 – 4:00 pm</p>
<p>WORK SESSION AGENDA</p>
<p>1.  DISCUSSION OF CAPITAL IMPROVEMENT PROJECTS FOR 2027-2029 AND THE 10-YEAR PLAN.</p>
<p>In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, individuals needing special accommodations (including auxiliary communicative aids and services) during this meeting should notify the Utah County Clerk’s Office at (801) 851-8113 at least two days prior to the meeting.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-620" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Provo Airport opens Snow-Removal Equipment Facility as part of Growth Plans</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 19, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PROVO, Utah — The Provo Airport opened a new snow-removal equipment building, a facility officials say will speed winter operations and help keep runways clear during storms.</p>
<p>“We have over 3,000,000 square feet of concrete and asphalt that needs to be snow plowed on a daily basis in a snowstorm,” Commissioner Beltran said. “This building will house all this equipment and it’s an awesome feature here at the Provo Airport.” He added that the project fits into a broader growth plan for the airport, which is moving from four gates to ten to accommodate increasing passengers, aircraft and services.</p>
<p>Beltran noted that July was “the best month ever” in the airport’s history, a trend he said continues with ongoing monthly records. He also highlighted the airport’s current reach: 16 nonstop destinations weekly with American Airlines, Allegiant and Breeze as partners, and he encouraged people to consider flying out of Provo. He said the airport’s proximity from car to gate—through security to the concourse—is smoother than at Salt Lake City International, calling the process a “very smooth, seamless” experience.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-604" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Community Development Block Grant Public Notice</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 18, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="/api/media/file/FONSI_NOI_RROF_for_Spring_Lake_with_Region_VIII_Contact_77a6d2fa03.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Spring Lake Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Community Development Block Grant Public Notice (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/FONSI_NOI_RROF_for_The_Refuge_with_Region_VIII_Contact_8e26b73568.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View The Refuge Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Community Development Block Grant Public Notice (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-618" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">250 Sleeping Mats Campaign</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 18, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>As part of our ongoing America 250 Celebration, we’re launching the “250 Sleeping Mats” community donation campaign, with a goal of providing 250 new sleeping mats for this year’s Utah County Warming Center before it opens on November 1.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-519" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">August 19, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 18, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1995" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about August 19, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/BOE_Agenda_2026_08_19_16b03d9531.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about August 19, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-609" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">August 19, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 17, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1897" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about August 19, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Commission_Agenda_2026_08_19_8146ea1639.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about August 19, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-602" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Notice of Vacancy - North Pointe Solid Waste Special Service District Control Board</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 17, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Notice is hereby provided this 12th day of August 2026, pursuant to Utah Code Section 17B-1-304 that one (1) vacancy currently exist on the North Pointe Solid Waste Special Service District Control Board (the “Board”). To be qualified for consideration for the above-mentioned Board vacancy, individuals must be a registered voter within the boundaries of the North Pointe Solid Waste Special Service District (the &quot;District&quot;).</p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice_2026_634_6ac2c87051.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Notice of Vacancy - North Pointe Solid Waste Special Service District Control Board (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-617" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Heather Eskelson August 2026 Employee of the Month</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 13, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>Heather Eskelson is Utah County&#x27;s Employee of the Month for August 2026. A little something about Heather...She goes out of her way to help her co-workers and willingly takes on extra tasks without being asked. She is patient with court patrons and her colleagues, staying calm and collected even in challenging situations. She has a great sense of humor and very creative, and she is consistently present and productive—she gets her work done quickly and is dependable and kind, making her a fantastic co-worker.</p>
<p>Heather is also an amazing UCEA board member. She is always willing to serve on the board and help where needed. UCEA cannot run without people who are willing to contribute to our activities, and Heather embodies that spirit.</p>
<p>Heather was recently promoted within the justice court due to her commitment and dedication to the citizens of Utah and other states. She is truly amazing at what she does. </p>
<p>Kim Love – Heather’s supervisor stated “I often tell Heather that I wish we could multiply her, like in the movie Multiplicity, because she is such a valuable part of the Justice Court team. She works well with every team member, is always pleasant, and I don’t think I’ve ever heard her complain. We know that she will complete any task she’s asked to do accurately and in a timely manner. I love listening to her conversations with our patrons; she is always kind, patient, and explains information in a way that patrons can understand and act on. She has been working with our front counter team, and we are excited for her to start collaborating with our in-court team. I am confident she will continue to do a great job there. Heather is definitely deserving of recognition as Employee of the Month.”</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-608" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">The June Sucker Recovery Program Keeps Water Flowing</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 11, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>WEST PROVO, Utah — Water continues to move through the Provo River Delta, despite drought conditions, a sign of decades of conservation work and multi-agency cooperation to support the recovery of the June Sucker fish and the broader health of Utah Lake.</p>
<p>Utah County Commissioner Skyler Beltran and Russ Franklin of Central Utah Water spoke during a visit to Provo Delta Gateway Park to highlight the ongoing efforts that keep water moving through the river and into the delta.</p>
<p>Franklin, who leads the charge at Central Utah Water, offered a look back at the June Sucker Recovery Program&#x27;s history. Since it began in 2002, he said, agencies across the state and federal partners have worked to secure water for the fish so it can access the Provo River and the delta.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-518" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">August 12, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 11, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1994" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about August 12, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/BOE_Agenda_2026_08_12_23b570a3ea.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about August 12, 2026 Board of Equalization of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-603" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Utah County Launches &quot;250 Sleeping Mats&quot; Community Donation Drive in Honor of America 250</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 10, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>UTAH COUNTY, Utah — As part of the ongoing America 250 celebration, Utah County is launching the &quot;250 Sleeping Mats&quot; community donation campaign, with a goal of providing 250 new sleeping mats for this year&#x27;s Utah County Warming Center before it opens on November 1.</p>
<p>The campaign offers residents a simple way to make a meaningful difference for some of the community&#x27;s most vulnerable neighbors. Community members can purchase a sleeping mat directly from Utah County’s Amazon Wish List, and it will be shipped straight to the facility for use during the upcoming warming center season.  <a href="https://bit.ly/4xBC0GP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://bit.ly/4xBC0GP<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
<p>Last winter, the Utah County Warming Center provided thousands of safe overnight stays for individuals experiencing homelessness, offering shelter from dangerous winter temperatures while connecting guests with critical support services. Sleeping mats are an essential part of creating a safe, comfortable, and dignified environment for those seeking refuge.</p>
<p>&quot;This donation campaign is a meaningful way for residents to help the community warming center and the people it serves,&quot; said Utah County Commission Chair Skyler Beltran. &quot;Our warming center program continues to improve each year as we make meaningful progress in reducing the number of community members experiencing homelessness. As we commemorate America&#x27;s 250th anniversary, this is an opportunity for all of us to demonstrate the spirit of service and compassion that has long defined our nation and our community.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Ensuring a safe and warm place for our most vulnerable community members is our top priority, and these sleeping mats are a tremendous help,&quot; said Heather Hogue, Program Manager for Mountainland Continuum of Care. &quot;Every donation directly supports individuals seeking shelter this winter and demonstrates the compassion that makes Utah County such a caring community.&quot;</p>
<p>The &quot;250 Sleeping Mats&quot; campaign reflects the spirit of America 250 by encouraging community members to give back through service. Organizers hope to collect all 250 mats before the warming center opens on November 1, ensuring every guest has a safe and comfortable place to sleep throughout the winter season.</p>
<p>Residents are encouraged to donate early and share the campaign with family, friends, businesses, and community organizations to help reach the goal of 250 sleeping mats before the start of the warming center season.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-596" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">August 12, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 10, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1896" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about August 12, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Commission_Agenda_2026_08_12_c2df8ff342.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about August 12, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-601" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Beware of Property Tax Disinformation Videos </h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">August 4, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>If you come across an animated video that looks like this...it’s click-bait.  It’s false.  Not true. It’s trying to trick you! </p>
<p>HERE ARE THE FACTS </p>
<p>• There is no federal law that grants property tax assessment caps based on age. Property taxes are governed by state and local governments, not the federal government. </p>
<p>• Claims about a federal mandate, a &quot;universal master form,&quot; or special tax benefits based on the decade you were born are disinformation from sensationalized online videos designed to generate clicks. </p>
<p>• No federal spending package has changed Utah&#x27;s local property tax laws. </p>
<p>Please do not be misled into watching these videos or purchasing unrelated financial products based on these false claims. </p>
<p>FOR UTAH PROPERTY OWNERS </p>
<p>• Utah does NOT have a senior property tax freeze program that locks in your home&#x27;s assessed value. </p>
<p>• Utah DOES offer a property tax reduction program known as the Circuit Breaker program for qualifying homeowners. Information about this program is available through the Auditor&#x27;s Office. </p>
<p>• Homeowners can also verify that their property receives the Primary Residential Exemption, which exempts 45% of your home&#x27;s fair market value from property taxes when the property is your primary residence, regardless of age or income. </p>
<p>IMPORTANT REMINDER</p>
<p>New Utah legislation requires a Residential Exemption form to be filed with the Assessor&#x27;s Office whenever there is a name change on a property. The form is available on our website. </p>
<p>Please be cautious about the information you share online and avoid providing personal information through &quot;unofficial&quot; forms or websites. If you have questions about your property&#x27;s assessment, exemptions, or available tax relief programs, click this link: auditor.utahcounty.gov/tax-relief </p>
<p>Our office is here to help. We encourage you to contact us directly so you can receive accurate, reliable information.</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-516" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">UC Tax Tourism Advisory Board Meeting </h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 31, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="/api/media/file/August_TTAB_Agenda_ae35346a1a.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about UC Tax Tourism Advisory Board Meeting  (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-504" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Utah County Fair Day 1</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 30, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>The first day of the Utah County Fair is in the books. Fun night!  Free Rodeo, Open Class &amp; 4-H judging was awesome! Commissioners Beltran, Gordon &amp; Powers Gardner selected their winners for the &quot;Commissioner&#x27;s Choice&quot; award.  Later that night...they waved to the packed house before the rodeo got underway. </p>
<p>Tonight is Utah County Employee night and the Monster Trucks extravaganza takes center stage!  We&#x27;ll see you there!</p>
<p>Thursday, July 30 · Fairgrounds open 2:00 PM to 10:00 PM</p>
<p>Friday, July 31 · Fairgrounds open 12:00 PM to 10:00 PM</p>
<p>Saturday, August 1 · Fairgrounds open 10:00 AM to 10:00 PM</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-514" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">July 30, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Special Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 29, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=2341" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about July 30, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Special Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Commission_Agenda_2026_07_30_5ed24f634b.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about July 30, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Special Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-595" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">July 30, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Special Commission Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 29, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=2341" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about July 30, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Special Commission Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Commission_Agenda_2026_07_30_a78f07a43d.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda<span class="sr-only"> about July 30, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Special Commission Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-600" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">The Uniformed and Overseas Citizens Absentee Voting Act (UOCAVA) Election Notice - July 24, 2026</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 23, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>The Uniformed and Overseas Citizens Absentee Voting Act (UOCAVA) Election Notice UCA 20A-16-502</p>
<p>July 24, 2026</p>
<p>Our records show you&#x27;re eligible to vote under the Uniformed and Overseas Citizens Absentee Voting Act (UOCAVA). You can vote in the upcoming election either with the ballot sent to you or by using a federal write-in absentee ballot (FWAB). <br/>
<!-- -->If you don’t receive a ballot in time to vote, you may complete a FWAB. When using a federal write-in absentee ballot, fill out the Voter Information section completely and accurately. Write in the office and candidate name(s) for the races you choose to vote for in the appropriate sections. Other Resources: <a href="http://www.overseasvotefoundation.org/vote/VoterInformation.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.overseasvotefoundation.org/vote/VoterInformation.htm<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/2026_UOCAVA_NOTICE_97a72cf636.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about The Uniformed and Overseas Citizens Absentee Voting Act (UOCAVA) Election Notice - July 24, 2026 (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-599" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Notice of Vacancy - Alpine Cove Water Special Service District Administrative Control Board</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 23, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>NOTICE OF VACANCY ON THE ALPINE COVE WATER SPECIAL SERVICE DISTRICT ADMINISTRATIVE CONTROL BOARD</p>
<p>Notice is hereby provided this 22nd day of July 2026, pursuant to Utah Code Section 178-1-304, that one (I) vacancy currently exists on the Alpine Cove Water Special Service District Administrative Control Board (the &quot;Board&quot;). To be qualified for consideration for the above-mentioned Board vacancy, the individual must be a registered voter within the boundaries of the Alpine Cove Water Special Service District (the &quot;District&quot;) or an officer or employee of Utah County.</p>
<p>Those individuals interested in being considered for the vacant Board position outlined above should send a letter expressing their interest, together with a brief description of their qualifications and eligibility for the Board position to: <a href="mailto:boards@utahcounty.gov">boards@utahcounty.gov</a>. All letters of interest in the vacant Board position must be received by the Board of County Commissioners, Utah County, Utah, on or before 5:00 p.m. on August 28th, 2026. The Board of County Commissioners, Utah County, Utah, will review and evaluate all individuals that qualify for consideration pursuant to the guidelines listed above and will appoint an individual to fill the existing Board vacancy by resolution. </p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice_2026_572_0e0c64602e.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Notice of Vacancy - Alpine Cove Water Special Service District Administrative Control Board (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-598" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Notice of Vacancies - Utah Valley Road Special Service District Administrative Control Board</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 23, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>NOTICE OF VACANCIES ON THE UTAH VALLEY ROAD SPECIAL SERVICE DISTRICT ADMINISTRATIVE CONTROL BOARD </p>
<p>Notice is hereby provided this 22nd day of July 2026, pursuant to Utah Code Section 178-1-304, that two (2) vacancies exist on the Utah Valley Road Special Service District Administrative Control Board. To qualify for consideration for the above-mentioned Board vacancies, individuals must be registered voters within the Utah Valley Road Special Service District, or an officer or employee of Utah County.<br/>
<!-- --> </p>
<p>Those individuals interested in being considered for the vacant Board positions outlined above should send a letter expressing their interest, together with a brief description of their qualifications and eligibility for the Board position to: <a href="mailto:boards@utahcounty.gov">boards@utahcounty.gov</a>. All letters of interest in the vacant Board positions must be received by the Board of County Commissioners, Utah County, Utah, on or before 5:00 p.m. on Friday, August 28, 2026. The Board of County Commissioners, Utah County, Utah, will review and evaluate all individuals that qualify for consideration pursuant to the guidelines listed above, and will appoint individuals to fill the existing Board vacancies by resolution. </p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/Notice_2026_571_3ed00791eb.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Notice<span class="sr-only"> about Notice of Vacancies - Utah Valley Road Special Service District Administrative Control Board (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-517" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">Fireworks over Utah Lake on Pioneer Day!</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 22, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><strong>Utah County, Utah</strong> — A drought-stricken Utah summer, a statewide fireworks ban, and a bold idea from local leaders have coalesced into Utah County’s inaugural America 250 Pioneer Day Celebration. The event, designed to honor both America’s founding and Utah’s pioneer heritage, will culminate in a fireworks display on Utah Lake on Pioneer Day.</p>
<p><strong>When:</strong> Friday, July 24, 10:00 p.m. - 10:30 p.m.</p>
<p><strong>Where:</strong> Utah Lake</p>
<p><em><strong>What to expect:</strong></em></p>
<ul>
<li>The celebration marks 250 years since America’s founding and honors pioneers past and present—from Utah’s early settlers to today’s entrepreneurs, educators, farmers, first responders, and public servants.</li>
<li>It’s a community-driven, countywide celebration born from a spirit of cooperation among state and local agencies, elected officials, first responders, county staff, businesses, sponsors, and residents.</li>
</ul>
<p><em><strong>Origin of Utah County’s America 250 Pioneer Day Celebration:</strong></em></p>
<p>Every tradition has an origin story. This one began during Utah’s driest summer in memory, when a statewide fireworks ban sought to protect lives and public lands. Yet the idea of celebrating resilience and community persisted.</p>
<p>“Pioneer Day is about remembering the courage and determination of those who came before us while celebrating the incredible place we get to call home. This event will give families across Utah County a memorable way to celebrate together and enjoy a truly spectacular show.” said Lehi City Councilwoman Emily Lockhart, who helped spark the plan.</p>
<p>Commissioner Skyler Beltran, Representative Stephanie Gricius and staff at the Utah Lake Authority joined Lockhart to reframe the moment. They envisioned a countywide celebration that would unite families from every corner of Utah County while honoring both our nation’s founding and Utah’s pioneer heritage.</p>
<p>“This all came together very quickly and will be a great community event that brings people to Utah Lake. A big thank you to the many businesses that helped make this possible, as well as the tremendous collaboration between our city, county and state partners,” - Beltran said.</p>
<p>What followed was an extraordinary collaboration. State and local agencies, elected officials, first responders, public safety personnel, county staff, businesses, sponsors, and countless citizens contributed time, expertise, and resources to make the celebration possible. The effort demonstrated that when a community rallies around a common purpose, remarkable things can happen.</p>
<p>The event honors the courage of the pioneers who settled Utah and the visionaries who founded the United States. It also recognizes today’s pioneers: entrepreneurs, educators, innovators, farmers, first responders, public servants, and families who continue to build thriving communities and expand opportunity for the next generation.</p>
<p>“As we celebrate Pioneer Day and America’s 250th anniversary, Fireworks at Utah Lake gives us an opportunity to come together as one community and celebrate the history, freedom, and pioneering spirit that have shaped both our state and our nation. This is the first year of what we hope will become a beloved Utah County tradition for generations to come, a night when families and neighbors from across the county gather around Utah Lake and celebrate together,” said Utah House of Representatives Stephanie Gricius.</p>
<p>That phone call between the three leaders on July 6 did more than launch an event. It launched a tradition built on the belief that even when circumstances change, Americans respond the way they always have: by coming together, solving problems, and creating something worthy of passing on.</p>
<p>Because America’s story has never been defined by what stands in its way. It has always been defined by what its people build together.</p>
<p>“We stand on the shoulders of pioneers. Their legacy is not only what they built, but the courage and grit they used to build. Our goal is to use that same pioneer spirit to create communities worthy of those who will one day stand on ours. Very beautiful.” said Nate Hutchinson Co Managing Partner of Utah City.</p>
<p><em><strong>Get more information:</strong></em> <a href="https://www.fireworksatutahlake.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.fireworksatutahlake.com<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
<p><em><strong>Frequently Asked Questions:</strong></em></p>
<ul>
<li>Can I watch from my boat? Yes. Boats are encouraged, but please follow all safety rules, including navigation lights, as it will be dark. The marinas will be charging their normal rates; check water levels before putting your boat in. The best location to watch from water is the western launch area near Saratoga Springs.</li>
<li>Can I watch from my paddleboard? No. Current laws do not allow non-motorized vessels on the lake after dark.</li>
<li>Best viewing from shore? The American Fork Marina is the primary spot, followed by Lindon Marina. Bring a blanket or chair and stay hydrated—it&#x27;s going to be warm.</li>
<li>On-water viewing? If you’re joining on the water, head to the western launch areas for optimal views.</li>
</ul>
<p><em><strong>Who Made This Possible:</strong></em></p>
<p>Thank you to our title sponsors, QTS and Utah City, for bringing the community together on Pioneer Day!</p></div></div></article><article id="notice-503" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">July 22, 2026 Utah County Community Reinvestment Agency Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 21, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p>PUBLIC NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN THAT THE</p>
<p><strong>UTAH COUNTY COMMUNITY REINVESTMENT AGENCY</strong></p>
<p>WILL HOLD A PUBLIC MEETING</p>
<p>IN THE COMMISSION CHAMBERS - ROOM 1400</p>
<p>OF THE UTAH COUNTY ADMINISTRATION BUILDING</p>
<p>100 E CENTER ST, PROVO, UT 84606</p>
<p><strong>July 22, 2026 - 2:00 PM</strong></p>
<p><a href="/api/media/file/07_22_2026_CRA_Agenda_70bface440.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="sr-only"> about July 22, 2026 Utah County Community Reinvestment Agency Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p></div></div></article><article id="notice-435" class="flex flex-col @3xl:gap-10 gap-4.5"><hr class="border-0 border-t border-gray-400"/><div><h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 text-xl leading-7">July 22, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting</h2><p class="mt-1 text-gray-500 text-sm leading-5">July 20, 2026</p><div class="mt-3 max-w-prose break-words content-flow"><p><a href="https://agenda.utahcounty.gov/agenda?id=1895" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agenda with Documents<span class="sr-only"> about July 22, 2026 Board of Commissioners of Utah County, Utah Public Meeting (opens in a new tab)</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" class="size-5 shrink-0" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M180-120q-24 0-42-18t-18-42v-600q0-24 18-42t42-18h279v60H180v600h600v-279h60v279q0 24-18 42t-42 18H180Zm202-219-42-43 398-398H519v-60h321v321h-60v-218L382-339Z"></path></svg></a></p>
